---
# Copy this file to <project>/.claude/appian-toolkit.local.md and adjust,
# then add `.claude/*.local.md` to that project's .gitignore.
#
# All fields are optional — delete any line to fall back to its default.
# The authoritative schema (every field, effect and default) is the table in
# ../SKILL.md § "Per-project settings". This template is a convenience copy:
# if the two ever disagree, the table wins.

# false → the WHOLE toolkit ignores this file, frontmatter and body alike,
# exactly as if it did not exist. Applies to the generator, the converter,
# the code reviewer and the reverse-engineering skill.
enabled: true

# Corporate palette (HEX, never "ACCENT"). A reference image in the request still wins.
brand_hex: null          # e.g. "#0050A0"
brand_hex_soft: null     # e.g. "#E6EEF7" (badges, hovers, soft backgrounds)

# Phase-2 data model markdown, relative to the project root.
data_model_context: "context/data-model-context.md"

# Where generated .sail files go, relative to the project root.
output_dir: "output"

# false → never generate a!chatField / a!callLanguageModel / a!agentChatField
# (requires Appian advanced/premium AI tier). Validators flag them as blocking.
ai_components_available: true

# Phase 2: prefer native a!kpiField over converted card KPIs when the
# decision rule in display-conversion-kpis.md § Pattern 0 allows it.
prefer_native_kpis: true

# appian-reverse-engineering: default depth when documenting an export.
# "onboarding" = the 11 standard deliverables.
# "rebuild"    = adds 10-especificacion/ (screen-by-screen spec, 100% rule
#                catalogue, state machines, user stories, traceability).
# When set, the skill uses it WITHOUT asking.
re_depth: "onboarding"
---

# Project notes (free-form — the generator reads this as context)

Describe here anything the generator should know about this project:
environment name, whose applications may be touched, naming prefixes,
verified capability notes (with date), UX conventions, etc.

Do NOT pin Appian version numbers in the frontmatter — when a feature's
availability matters, verify it at generation time via the appian-docs MCP
or appian-dev validateExpression().
